# Sample requests for RevisionTrack (Week 2: authentication added).
# Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (click "Send Request" above a request).
# Run `python seed.py` first. Seeded ids for the demo user: clients 1-3, projects 1-4, revision requests 1-7.
# Project 5, client 4 and revision request 8 belong to the second user (useful for 403 tests).

@base = http://127.0.0.1:5000

### ---------- AUTH ----------

### Register a new user -> 201 (the password is never returned)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "new_freelancer", "email": "new@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

### Register with an email that is already taken -> 409
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "someone_else", "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

### Register with a weak password -> 400
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "weak_user", "email": "weak@example.com", "password": "short" }

### Login with the wrong password -> 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "WrongPassword1" }

### Login as the demo user -> 200 with an access token
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

##List Projects
GET {{base}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
### ---------- CLIENTS ----------

### List my clients
GET {{base}}/clients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a client -> 201
POST {{base}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "Harbour Books", "email": "orders@harbourbooks.example.com" }

### Create the same client again -> 409
POST {{base}}/clients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "Harbour Books", "email": "orders@harbourbooks.example.com" }

### Get one client
GET {{base}}/clients/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a client
PATCH {{base}}/clients/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "Sunrise Bakery Ltd" }

### Another user's client -> 403
GET {{base}}/clients/4
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A client's projects (relationship)
GET {{base}}/clients/1/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a client -> 204 (its projects are kept, with no client)
DELETE {{base}}/clients/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- PROJECTS ----------

### List my projects
GET {{base}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a project -> 201
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "title": "Shop sign design", "description": "Sign for the front window", "client_id": 1, "agreed_revisions": 2 }

### Create a project with invalid data -> 400
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "title": "", "agreed_revisions": -1, "status": "Done" }

### Create a project for someone else's client -> 400
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "title": "Sneaky project", "client_id": 4, "agreed_revisions": 1 }

### Get one project
GET {{base}}/projects/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a project
PATCH {{base}}/projects/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "status": "Completed", "agreed_revisions": 4 }

### Detach a project from its client
PATCH {{base}}/projects/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "client_id": null }

### Another user's project -> 403
GET {{base}}/projects/5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a project -> 204 (its revision requests are deleted too)
DELETE {{base}}/projects/4
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- REVISION REQUESTS ----------

### Log a request (project 1 has a limit of 3 and 2 used, so this one is not extra)
POST {{base}}/projects/1/revision-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "description": "Use a thinner font for the tagline" }

### Log another (limit used up, so is_extra becomes true)
POST {{base}}/projects/1/revision-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "description": "Also add a version for dark backgrounds" }

### Log a request with the wrong fields -> 400
POST {{base}}/projects/1/revision-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "description": "Sneaky", "is_extra": false }

### Log a request on someone else's project -> 403
POST {{base}}/projects/5/revision-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "description": "This should be blocked" }

### List a project's requests
GET {{base}}/projects/2/revision-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List filtered by status
GET {{base}}/projects/2/revision-requests?status=Pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one request
GET {{base}}/revision-requests/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update status
PATCH {{base}}/revision-requests/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "status": "Completed" }

### Update with an invalid status -> 400
PATCH {{base}}/revision-requests/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "status": "Done" }

### Delete a request -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/revision-requests/7
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Request that does not exist -> 404
GET {{base}}/revision-requests/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
